# LV2 syscalls the ELF makes, one number per line (tools/syscalls.py checks the
# ELF against this file; --write rewrites it from a known-good ELF and drops
# these notes). Written on 2026-10-09 from the 2.0.1 tree: 45 numbers, 95 call
# sites, cross-checked against ppu-objdump (every sc resolved).
# The app's own calls are named in README.md (Safety, How it reaches the
# drive): 383 temperatures, 409 fan duty, 600/601/609/616 the drive. The rest
# is PSL1GHT's runtime: threads and time (44, 141, 142, 145, 146), memory
# (330, 331, 337), the tty (402, 403), the network (700 to 714) and the file
# system (801 to 834). Never 602, 604 or 870: the script refuses them whatever
# this file says.
